# Generated by the deploy CLI (`./deploy/cc up`). Contains owner-password-
# equivalent secrets (currently: auto-generated DEFAULT_OWNER_PASSWORD when
# the user pressed Enter at the "leave blank to auto-generate" prompt). Must
# NOT be committed — keep this file alongside `.env` (which is also excluded
# from git) and any other deployment-specific secrets.
.cc-credentials.txt

# Per-deployment state file produced by the wizard. Contains resource IDs
# (Telnyx voice-app / SIP / OVP IDs) but no secrets; gitignored so every
# developer / CI run generates its own.
.cc-state.json

# Local docker-compose .env. Same rationale as .env in any other project —
# each developer / deployment gets their own, and committing it would leak
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD / NEXTAUTH_SECRET / TELNYX_API_KEY.
.env

# Timestamped backups written by `./deploy/cc clean` (which snapshots every
# wizard artifact — .cc-state.json, .cc-credentials.txt, terraform.tfstate,
# etc. — before deleting the originals, so a mistaken clean is recoverable).
# Each backup is a self-contained snapshot that can safely be removed once
# the operator is sure no restore is needed.
.cc-backups/

# Cloudflare quick-tunnel log (see lib/tunnel.mjs). Regenerated on every
# `cc up` that auto-starts a tunnel; not useful across runs.
.cc-tunnel.log

# Durable side-channel cache for one-time Telnyx secrets (currently
# TELNYX_AI_API_KEY) that can never be read back after creation — see
# lib/telnyx-secrets-cache.mjs. Contains a live secret; gitignored like
# .cc-credentials.txt / .env.
.cc-telnyx-secrets.json
